Section 1 - Definitions

a. TEMPORAL means the software in the repository https://github.com/AllastorV/temporal and in its releases: source code, binaries, installers, documentation and assets such as logos, icons, presets and demo media.

b. Derivative means any work that is based on or incorporates TEMPORAL and that is translated, altered, arranged, transformed, adapted, ported or otherwise modified, including a fork, and including a plugin or program that contains a substantial part of TEMPORAL's code or assets. A host application that loads TEMPORAL through the OpenFX interface, such as DaVinci Resolve, and a project file that uses TEMPORAL are not Derivatives.

c. Licensor means Alastor (https://github.com/AllastorV), the individual who grants rights under this license.

d. You means the individual or entity exercising the rights granted under this license.

e. Share means to provide TEMPORAL or a Derivative to any other person by any means, including copying, distributing, publishing and making available for download.

f. Output means images, video, audio, data and any other media that You create by running TEMPORAL. Output does not include TEMPORAL itself or any part of TEMPORAL's code or assets.

g. Charge means any money or other thing of value asked for or required in exchange.

h. Hosted Service means a service that gives other people access to the functions of TEMPORAL or of a Derivative over a network. Doing work for a client with TEMPORAL and delivering the Output to the client is not a Hosted Service, even when the client pays for the work.


